# Mobile presentation order

On viewports below `lg` (max-width 1023px), stacked page and section content must appear in this order:

1. Headline (eyebrow may sit immediately above it)
2. Image
3. Body / text content
4. CTA button

Skip a slot if that block does not exist. Do not add filler.

Desktop layouts may keep side-by-side or overlay compositions. Do not change desktop order to satisfy this rule.

Source order should match the mobile visual order so reading order stays correct. Use CSS grid placement (`lg:col-start-*`) to rearrange for desktop. Do not use `order` as the only mobile solution when the DOM can be structured correctly.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — mobile stacks headline → image → body → CTA
<div className="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <h2 className="lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-1">Headline</h2>
  <img className="lg:col-start-1 lg:row-span-3" alt="" src="..." />
  <p className="lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-2">Body copy.</p>
  <a className="lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-3" href="/enter">Enter the Contest</a>
</div>

// ❌ BAD — mobile shows image or CTA before the headline
<div>
  <img alt="" src="..." />
  <h2>Headline</h2>
  <a href="/enter">Enter the Contest</a>
  <p>Body copy.</p>
</div>
```

This applies to every public page and marketing section, including the homepage hero, about, and closing CTA. Icon-only list items (for example How to Enter steps) are not this pattern.
